    "Requirement Analysis": "We must implement a Java 11 Maven project with a thin Main, a single JUnit 5 test file, and a set of domain and service classes that exactly match the specified contracts. Java record syntax is forbidden under Java 11; both entities must be declared as public final class. We must repeat and enforce: User constructor stores raw values unchanged and never validates; UserValidator performs validation and repository.save throws IllegalArgumentException for invalid input; SearchService performs exact case-insensitive whitespace-delimited token matching of names and preserves input order, returning defensive copies; Audit logging is explicit and decoupled from repository; repository supports deterministic upsert and defensive list returns; default package usage; strict direct imports of java.util types; Main.java contains no collections and must include the standalone call searchService.search(repository.findAll(), \"alice\");. pom.xml must declare org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter (scope test) and a Maven Surefire version that runs JUnit 5. Tests must be deterministic with exactly three @Test methods covering: (1) runtime plus value-object getters/equality with fixed timestamp 1640995200000L; (2) validation false for new User(\"\", null, \"\") and search of [Alice Smith, Bob Jones] by \"smith\" returns only Alice; (3) CRUD upsert and delete with explicit AuditLogService.log of CREATE_USER and DELETE_USER and assertions of exactly those two events.\n\nConcrete design and implementation tasks for every file (ordered by dependency):\n1) pom.xml\n- Task: Configure Maven for Java 11; add junit-jupiter dependency (scope test) and maven-surefire-plugin version compatible with JUnit 5; no extra non-test deps; ensure test command mvn -q test runs JUnit Jupiter.\n\n2) src/main/java/User.java\n- Task: Implement public final class User with private final String id, name, email; constructor User(String id, String name, String email) stores args unchanged; provide getters getId/getName/getEmail; implement value-based equals, hashCode (all fields), and toString; no validation; no imports of java.util unless needed (none here).\n\n3) src/main/java/AuditEvent.java\n- Task: Implement public final class AuditEvent with private final long timestamp and private final String action, userId; validating constructor (reject null/blank action/userId; allow any long timestamp); getters getTimestamp/getAction/getUserId; value-based equals/hashCode/toString; import java.util.Objects if used and include direct import when referenced.\n\n4) src/main/java/UserValidator.java\n- Task: Stateless class with boolean isValid(User user) returning false for null user or null/blank id/name/email; true otherwise; never throws; include helper isBlank(String) if needed.\n\n5) src/main/java/SearchService.java\n- Task: Stateless class with List<User> search(List<User> users, String query); direct imports for java.util.List and java.util.ArrayList; behavior: if users is null, return new empty list; if query is null/blank, return defensive copy of users; else trim/lower-case query and include users whose non-null name contains a whitespace-delimited token equal to the query (tokenize by one-or-more whitespace), preserve input order, never mutate input; return new list.\n\n6) src/main/java/AuditLogService.java\n- Task: Maintain internal list of AuditEvent; methods: void log(AuditEvent event) that validates non-null event and appends; List<AuditEvent> getAllEvents() returning a defensive copy; import java.util.List and java.util.ArrayList; no static/global state.\n\n7) src/main/java/UserRepository.java\n- Task: Interface must literally begin with `import java.util.List;` then `public interface UserRepository`; declare methods: User findById(String id); List<User> findAll(); User save(User user); boolean deleteById(String id); Javadoc each method's contract (null handling, defensive copies, upsert behavior). No package declaration.\n\n8) src/main/java/InMemoryUserRepository.java\n- Task: Implement UserRepository; use private final Map<String, User> store (import java.util.Map, java.util.HashMap); use private final UserValidator validator; constructor initializes store and validator; save(User) validates via validator and throws IllegalArgumentException if invalid; on valid input, upsert by id and return stored value; findById returns value or null; findAll returns new ArrayList<>(store.values()) preserving deterministic order – use insertion order by backing store with LinkedHashMap if order is material; since only order preservation is required relative to input operations, prefer LinkedHashMap (import java.util.LinkedHashMap) to ensure stable iteration order; deleteById returns true if removed; never expose internal collections; import java.util.List and java.util.ArrayList directly where referenced.\n\n9) src/main/java/Main.java\n- Task: Thin, non-interactive demo in default package; no java.util imports; create repository, validator implicitly via InMemoryUserRepository, create a SearchService and invoke searchService.search(repository.findAll(), \"alice\"); as a standalone expression, without storing result; create a couple of Users and perform save/delete to exercise runtime wiring; ensure no collection type declarations or variables are present.\n\n10) src/test/java/MainTest.java\n- Task: JUnit Jupiter test class with exactly three @Test methods:\n  (1) Runtime + value objects: construct User and AuditEvent with timestamp 1640995200000L and assert getters and value-based equality and toString/equals consistency; also ensure Main.main(new String[0]) runs without exception.\n  (2) Validation + search: assert new User(\"\", null, \"\") is invalid; build users [new User(\"1\",\"Alice Smith\",\"alice@example.com\"), new User(\"2\",\"Bob Jones\",\"bob@example.com\")] and search for \"smith\"; assert only Alice is returned; ensure SearchService handles case-insensitive token logic.\n  (3) CRUD + explicit audit: use InMemoryUserRepository to upsert id \"1\" then delete it; construct AuditLogService, explicitly log two AuditEvent entries with fixed timestamp 1640995200000L and actions CREATE_USER and DELETE_USER for userId \"1\"; assert getAllEvents returns exactly those two events in order; assert repository operations did not implicitly log.\n- Imports: JUnit Jupiter assertions and annotations; java.util.List and java.util.ArrayList only where required; no reflection, no record component syntax.\n\nThese tasks adhere to the strict import rules (`import java.util.List;` requirement), the Main.java no-collection-declaration rule and standalone search call usage, the non-validating User constructor with separate validator, the exact name-token search rule with the Alice/Bob fixture, the explicit non-coupled audit rule, the upsert rule, the exactly-three-test rule, and the fixed fixtures, and explicitly maintain that public final class User and public final class AuditEvent are used while Java record syntax is forbidden under Java 11.",
