    "Full API spec": "Build: pom.xml\n- Declares Java 11 source/target. Adds dependency org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter (scope test) and configures maven-surefire-plugin (JUnit 5 compatible, e.g., 2.22.2+). No non-test dependencies. Running `mvn -q test` executes JUnit Jupiter tests.\n\nsrc/main/java/User.java\n- public final class User\n  - Fields: private final String id, name, email.\n  - Constructor: public User(String id, String name, String email)\n    - Stores arguments unchanged (may be null/blank). No validation here.\n  - Methods:\n    - public String getId()\n    - public String getName()\n    - public String getEmail()\n    - public boolean equals(Object o): value-based: compares id, name, email.\n    - public int hashCode(): consistent with equals.\n    - public String toString(): includes field values for diagnostics; exact format not tested.\n  - Semantics: Typed stored domain object with value semantics. Java record syntax is forbidden under Java 11.\n\nsrc/main/java/AuditEvent.java\n- public final class AuditEvent\n  - Fields: private final long timestamp; private final String action; private final String userId.\n  - Constructor: public AuditEvent(long timestamp, String action, String userId)\n    - Validates action and userId are non-null and non-blank; throws IllegalArgumentException otherwise.\n    - timestamp is stored as-is without validation.\n  - Methods:\n    - public long getTimestamp()\n    - public String getAction()\n    - public String getUserId()\n    - public boolean equals(Object o): value-based: compares timestamp, action, userId.\n    - public int hashCode(): consistent with equals.\n    - public String toString(): includes field values; exact format not tested.\n  - Semantics: Typed stored domain object with validating constructor. Java record syntax is forbidden under Java 11.\n\nsrc/main/java/UserValidator.java\n- public final class UserValidator\n  - Methods:\n    - public boolean isValid(User user)\n      - Returns false for null user or if any of user.getId(), user.getName(), or user.getEmail() is null or blank (after trimming).\n      - Returns true otherwise.\n  - Error behavior: Never throws; strictly returns boolean.\n\nsrc/main/java/SearchService.java\n- public final class SearchService\n  - Imports: direct imports for java.util.List and java.util.ArrayList.\n  - Methods:\n    - public List<User> search(List<User> users, String query)\n      - If users == null: returns new empty ArrayList<>.\n      - If query is null or blank after trimming: returns a defensive copy of users (never returns the original list object; if users is non-null, copy preserves order; if users is null, previous rule applies).\n      - Otherwise: let q = lower-case trimmed query; for each non-null User in users, split user.getName() (null-safe treat as empty) on whitespace; include the user if any token lower-cased equals q. Preserves input order. Never mutates input list or user objects.\n  - Semantics: Exact case-insensitive whitespace-delimited name token matching; the fixture [\"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\"] queried with \"smith\" returns only Alice Smith.\n\nsrc/main/java/AuditLogService.java\n- public final class AuditLogService\n  - Imports: direct imports for java.util.List and java.util.ArrayList.\n  - Fields: private final List<AuditEvent> events = new ArrayList<>();\n  - Methods:\n    - public void log(AuditEvent event)\n      - Appends non-null event to the internal list. If event is null, no-op (defensive behavior).\n    - public List<AuditEvent> getAllEvents()\n      - Returns a new ArrayList<>(events), i.e., a defensive copy in insertion order.\n  - Semantics: Independent explicit log; no static/global state.\n\nsrc/main/java/UserRepository.java\n- Import rule: The file must literally begin with `import java.util.List;`.\n- public interface UserRepository\n  - Methods:\n    - User findById(String id)\n      - Returns stored User for id or null if absent.\n    - List<User> findAll()\n      - Returns a defensive list copy preserving insertion/upsert order.\n    - User save(User user)\n      - Validates via UserValidator; throws IllegalArgumentException if invalid. On valid input, performs deterministic upsert by user.getId(): inserts if new id, replaces prior value if id exists. Returns stored value.\n    - boolean deleteById(String id)\n      - Removes entry by id; returns true if an entry was removed, false otherwise.\n  - Semantics: Repository boundary with CRUD method contracts; strict import rule at file start. Callers must not rely on implicit auditing.\n\nsrc/main/java/InMemoryUserRepository.java\n- public final class InMemoryUserRepository implements UserRepository\n  - Imports: java.util.List, java.util.ArrayList, java.util.Map, java.util.LinkedHashMap (and optionally java.util.Objects if used).\n  - Fields:\n    - private final LinkedHashMap<String, User> store = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n    - private final UserValidator validator = new UserValidator();\n  - Constructor: public InMemoryUserRepository()\n  - Methods:\n    - public User findById(String id): returns store.get(id) or null.\n    - public List<User> findAll(): returns new ArrayList<>(store.values()), preserving insertion/upsert order.\n    - public User save(User user): if validator.isValid(user) is false, throws IllegalArgumentException; else store.put(user.getId(), user) and return the stored value.\n    - public boolean deleteById(String id): returns store.remove(id) != null.\n  - Semantics: Deterministic upsert by id; defensive list returns; never exposes internal storage; does not perform any implicit logging.\n\nsrc/main/java/Main.java\n- public final class Main\n  - Methods:\n    - public static void main(String[] args)\n      - Thin non-interactive demo: constructs InMemoryUserRepository and SearchService; creates/saves a couple of Users; includes the standalone call `searchService.search(repository.findAll(), \"alice\");` as an expression without storing the result; deletes one id; exits. No collection type declaration or usage in source; no java.util imports.\n  - Semantics: Environment-dependent bootstrap only; no loops or I/O required by tests.\n\nsrc/test/java/MainTest.java\n- JUnit Jupiter test file; exactly three @Test methods.\n  1) Runtime + value objects\n     - Constructs new User(\"x\",\"y\",\"z\") and new AuditEvent(1640995200000L, \"ACT\", \"x\"); asserts getters and value-based equality; invokes Main.main(new String[0]) to ensure runtime wiring.\n  2) Validation + search\n     - Asserts new UserValidator().isValid(new User(\"\", null, \"\")) is false.\n     - Creates list [new User(\"1\",\"Alice Smith\",\"alice@example.com\"), new User(\"2\",\"Bob Jones\",\"bob@example.com\")], runs new SearchService().search(list, \"smith\"); asserts result contains only the Alice user and preserves order.\n  3) CRUD + explicit audit\n     - Uses InMemoryUserRepository to upsert id \"1\" and then delete it; asserts deleteById returns true; constructs AuditLogService, logs two AuditEvent entries with timestamp 1640995200000L and actions CREATE_USER and DELETE_USER for userId \"1\"; asserts getAllEvents() returns exactly those two events in order and verifies no implicit logging occurred.\n\nGlobal import and syntax constraints\n- UserRepository.java must literally begin with `import java.util.List;`.\n- Every file that uses List, ArrayList, Map, HashMap, LinkedHashMap, or Objects must import that type directly and must never rely on transitive imports.\n- Main.java must not declare or reference any collection types and must include the standalone call `searchService.search(repository.findAll(), \"alice\");`.\n- Java record syntax is forbidden under Java 11; both User and AuditEvent are ordinary public final classes with private final fields and getters.\n- User constructor never validates; UserValidator performs validation; repository.save validates and throws IllegalArgumentException on invalid input.\n- Search rule: exact case-insensitive whitespace-delimited name-token matching; the Alice Smith/Bob Jones fixture with query \"smith\" returns only Alice Smith.\n- AuditLogService is explicit and decoupled from repository operations; tests must log events explicitly.\n- Tests are deterministic, headless, and use JUnit Jupiter only, with exactly three @Test methods.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "All classes reside in the default package under src/main/java with no package declarations to avoid import mismatches. Build uses Maven with Java 11 and JUnit Jupiter via Surefire. Import rules are strict: every file using java.util types must import them directly. UserRepository.java literally begins with `import java.util.List;`. Main.java contains no collection declarations and includes the standalone call to SearchService: `searchService.search(repository.findAll(), \"alice\");`. Tests in src/test/java/MainTest.java (JUnit 5) cover runtime wiring, value object equality/getters, validation + search behavior, and CRUD + explicit audit with fixed timestamps; repository operations never log implicitly.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Test command: mvn -q test. Runtime entry: src/main/java/Main.java. Single protocol-level test file: src/test/java/MainTest.java containing exactly three @Test methods. Tests are headless, deterministic, and offline. Additional implementation files do not alter protocol files. No GUI or network is used. All modules compile under Java 11 without preview features.",
